💡 **SUGGESTION: Duplicated module loader + unused first load in test 1**

This test loads the module twice: the `loadActionModule(tracker)` result on line 84 is never used, and the IIFE below re-inlines the exact `makeRequire` map that `loadActionModule` already encapsulates — only to pass a recording `assignStub`, which the helper's second parameter already supports:

```js
var mod = loadActionModule(tracker);          // ← unused
...
var assignMod = (function() {                 // ← duplicates loadActionModule
    return loadModule(
        'js/createSolutionDesignTicketsAndAssignForReview.js',
        makeRequire({ ...same map as loadActionModule... }),
        {}
    );
})();
```

Simpler and drift-proof:

```js
var seenAssign = [];
var assignStub = function(ticketKey, initiatorId, wipLabel, targetStatus, tr) {
    seenAssign.push([ticketKey, initiatorId, wipLabel, targetStatus, tr]);
    return { success: true };
};
var mod = loadActionModule(tracker, assignStub);
var result = mod.action(makeParams(...));
```

The inline copy will silently diverge if the module gains a new `require` (the helper's map gets updated, this one doesn't). No behavior change intended — test-only cleanup.

💡 **SUGGESTION: Dead test variable — `seen` is never read**

```js
var seen = [];
var gh = loadGithubHelpers({ ... });
var result = gh.fetchDiscussionsAndRawData('org', 'repo', '5');
seen.push(result);
assert.equal(result.markdown, null);
...
```

`seen` accumulates one push and is never asserted on — left over from an earlier draft. The assertions on `result` already cover the behavior; drop `seen` (and the push) to keep the test honest about what it checks.

💡 **SUGGESTION: Characterize the all-markers edge of the general-comments section**

This suite pins the marker-skip behavior for a mixed comment list, but stops one edge short: when **every** general comment is a `<!-- dmtools: ... -->` marker, `buildGeneralCommentsSection` still returns the `## General PR Comments` header, so the caller pushes the section and `markdown` comes back **non-null with zero visible comments**. This is preserved pre-extraction behavior (the old inline code did the same), so nothing regressed — but a one-line characterization test would lock that contract in and document it for consumers of `fetchDiscussionsAndRawData` (`preparePRForReview`, `preCliReworkSetup`, `postStoryTestAutomationReviewHelpers`), which currently treat non-null `markdown` as "has discussion content".

```js
test('all-marker comments still yield a header-only section (preserved behavior)', function() {
    var gh = ghWith([
        { user: { login: 'bot' }, created_at: '2026-03-26T10:00:00Z',
          body: '<!-- dmtools:naked-pr-rearm {"pr":7} --> rearm' }
    ]);
    var result = gh.fetchDiscussionsAndRawData('org', 'repo', '7');
    assert.ok(result.markdown, 'header-only section keeps markdown non-null');
    assert.contains(result.markdown, '## General PR Comments');
    assert.notContains(result.markdown, 'naked-pr-rearm');
});
```

Optional — coverage deepening only, no action required for this PR.

