``
NEW:
```js
function extractCommentBody(comment) {
   if (!comment) return '';
   var body = comment.body;
   if (typeof body === 'string') return body;
   var structured = extractStructuredCommentBody(body);
   if (structured !== null) return structured;
   return JSON.stringify(body);
}
``

extractStructuredCommentBody:
```js
function extractStructuredCommentBody(body) {
   if (!body) return null;
   for (var i = 0; i < COMMENT_BODY_REPRESENTATIONS.length; i++) {
       var repr = body[COMMENT_BODY_REPRESENTATIONS[i]];
       if (repr && typeof repr.value === 'string') return repr.value;
   }
   return null;
}
``

Semantic equivalence check for weird `body` values:
- body = null/undefined/false/''/0 → old: skips ifs, JSON.stringify(body). new: extractStructuredCommentBody returns null → JSON.stringify(body). Same. ✓
- body = 'string' → returned earlier. ✓
- body = number 7 → old: `body && body.storage` → 7 truthy, 7.storage = undefined → falsy → skip → JSON.stringify(7) = '7'. New: loop: body['storage'] = undefined → repr falsy → skip; ... → null → JSON.stringify(7) = '7'. Same. ✓
